course: dictionary
lesson: 2722
title: Dinner: one word, many meals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dinner usually means the main meal of the day, but the place, the time and the people with you can change what it means. Context clues in the sentence show you which meaning fits. «The night before, the whole family folds dumplings together and eats the reunion dinner» tells you it is a big family meal, eaten at night.
explain: Read the words around dinner. «Dinner time» at home means a meal with your family, and words like «table manners» and «say please and thank you» help you picture it. At school in the UK, «school dinners» are the lunchtime meal, so the clue is the time of day and the place.
explain: Be careful in the UK, Ireland and Australia: dinner can mean the midday meal, and the evening meal is called tea. If a friend says, «Let's have dinner at twelve», they mean lunch. Always check the time of the meal. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to test it.
fact: Dinner is the main meal of the day, usually eaten in the evening.
fact: In some parts of the UK, Ireland and Australia, dinner means the midday meal, which is lunch.
fact: A dinner can also be a formal party with a meal, as in «dinner party».
fact: Dinner as a meal is uncountable: you have dinner, but a dinner is a formal party.
fact: Phrases to know: «have dinner», «make dinner», «dinner is ready», «dinner party», «school dinners», «dinner ladies».
exercise: «Ollie tried out a new word at Sunday dinner.» What does dinner mean here? | The helpers who look after children at school | A snack eaten in the morning | A formal party with dancing | *A family meal at home
exercise: At school in the UK, «school dinners» are which meal? | A bedtime snack | *Lunch, in the middle of the day | Tea at six o'clock | Breakfast
exercise: What is a «dinner party»? | *A formal party with a meal | A race for dinner ladies | A party with no food at all | A small snack eaten standing up
test: In Sydney, a friend says, «Let's have dinner at twelve o'clock.» What meal do they mean? | Supper at night | Breakfast | Afternoon tea | *Lunch
test: «The whole family eats the reunion dinner on New Year's Eve.» What does dinner mean here? | A formal party only | *A big family meal eaten together | A cup of tea | A school lunch
exam: In «Let's have dinner at twelve», which context clue tells you dinner means lunch? | Dinner is always uncountable | The word friend shows it is informal | *The time, twelve o'clock, which is in the middle of the day | The word dinner has the letter y in it
